  "worked_solution": "Let's examine each of our numbers in turn.\n\n- $3.624$ is a rational number because it can be expressed as a ratio of two integers:\n\n$$\n3.624=\\frac{3\\,624}{1\\,000}\n$$\n\n- $0.\\overset{―}{25}$ is a rational number. The notation $\\overset{―}{25}$ tells us that the digits $2$ and $5$ after the decimal point repeat indefinitely.\n\n$$\n0.\\overset{―}{25}=0.2525252525…\n$$\n\nAny decimal with repeating digits can be represented as a ratio of two integers. In this case,\n\n$$\n0.\\overset{―}{25}=\\frac{25}{99}.\n$$\n\n- $7.526380…$ is not a rational number. The notation \"$…$\" tells us that digits after the decimal point extend forever. However, there are no repeating digits.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\"",
